 {"id":"fabro-22e4","title":"agent: edit-tool file writes land with mtime 1970-01-01 — cargo skips recompiles, edits silently lag until manual touch","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.569Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:51:48.005Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"From unreviewed run 01M1Y2SMEVDHAFB59GZV9B84CQ (PR #41 implementer; recovered via journal sweep 2026-09-07 after the run aged out of revisor freshness): edit-tool file writes landed with mtime 1970-01-01 (e.g. lib/components/fabro-validate/src/file_refs.rs), so cargo considered the sources older than cached rlibs and silently skipped recompiles — a just-added pub fn was reported missing and behavior lagged the edits until a manual touch. This is silent cache poisoning of the build loop: any agent edit can produce a stale-binary diagnosis that costs implementer revisits. Fix direction: the platform's file-write path (edit tool / sandbox write transport) must set a real mtime — utimensat/write-with-times after creating or replacing the file so downstream build systems see fresh sources. Acceptance: an edit-tool write produces mtime == wall clock (unit test on the write path); a before/after cargo check in a scratch crate recompiles after an agent edit without manual touch.","labels":["engine","agent"],"closedAt":"2026-09-07T18:51:48.005Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-b8ed","title":"develop: verification-only briefs must not assert 'criteria satisfied' — derive per-criterion checks instead","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.670Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.670Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"From unreviewed run 01M1Y852BN91NSVSHFWNWTW5ST (PR #42; journal sweep 2026-09-07): the verification-only brief asserted 'acceptance criteria appear already satisfied', but criterion 5 of fabro-5e09 was materially unmet in the worktree — docs/agents/issue-tracker.md still said 'Filers assign at creation' and 'Assignment is a user decision', contradicting the seed's D2/D3 decisions from the same day. The pass only converged because the implementer re-checked; a lazier one would have closed the seed on the brief's word. Fix direction: the planner's verification-only brief generation must not carry satisfaction assertions — instead list each acceptance criterion with an instruction to verify it against the CURRENT worktree and report per-criterion status in the summary. Related: fabro-578a (different aspect: allowed command level in verification-only briefs).","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-52a9","title":"conductor survey: reword misleading 'burns the backlog down' claim — backlog journal is visibility-only, drain needs the revisor's newest-first rule to change","status":"open","type":"task","priority":3,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.771Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T18:30:04.771Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"PR #45's survey prompt says 'the revisor revises the newest revisable run, so each subsequent pass burns the backlog down one run at a time' — but the revise leg creates the revisor without a goal and the revisor's select rule picks the NEWEST unrevised fresh run (which is always the current pass's own child), so the backlog NEVER drains; additionally the freshness rule (ADR-0015) makes older runs stale-evidence the moment the workflow version drifts, permanently disqualifying them. The journal line is dead-letter optimism (user + agent analysis 2026-09-07). Fix: reword survey.md to state the truth — the backlog entry is VISIBILITY-only (unreviewed run ids stay observable), runs are only revisable while fresh, and a real drain would need the revise leg to pass an explicit backlog run id in the goal (a decision not made). Do not promise behavior the graph cannot deliver.","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
-{"id":"fabro-2254","title":"Mirror the gate's default-features clippy in the implementer's pre-gate check","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T18:58:15.104Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T19:19:56.648Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md step 4, require the literal gate invocation cargo clippy -p <crate> --all-targets -- -D warnings (default features) on every touched crate in addition to any feature-scoped checks, and make a known default-features break FAIL the 'gate passes' criterion. In run 01M1YJ8R820R7ZMSN55GJGMZ4A the implementer verified only under --features docker while the default-features E0432 it had itself diagnosed red-lined the tester 11s in, forcing a full second cycle (~8 min, ~$0.41, 64% of run cost). Distinct from closed fabro-0d56 (crate scoping): this is feature-set parity. Basis: run 01M1YJ8R820R7ZMSN55GJGMZ4A, workflow version 4ff76f32665f954e9a8e2027ec2a4a5b48266707730ae0620fcfd3f79acd4a10, commit b1dbce3b713540dc605bec39d9ac09c17a224cb4","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
